{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>היליכי.</b> She prophesied and did not know what she prophesied — הֵי שֶׁלִּיכִי."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Rashi glosses Pharaoh's daughter's word היליכי ('go [you all]') as unwitting prophecy, for through it the infant Moses was returned to his own people. הֵי שֶׁלִּיכִי renders the Hebrew form in the feminine singular imperative with final meaning 'walk, go.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:14.325396192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}